<title>SPAIN: Acerinox to cut share nominal, pay back cash.</title>
<headline>Acerinox to cut share nominal, pay back cash.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish steel firm Acerinox said on Wednesday it would reduce the nominal value of its shares to 800 pesetas from 900 pesetas, paying back the difference to shareholders.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the firm said it would also return cash from an issue premium account to shareholders, although he declined to specify what the amount would be.</p>
<p>The move is to be proposed to the forthcoming shareholders' meeting.  </p>
<p>The spokesman said the issue premium account in total stands at 21.0 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
